        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0740" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1946v04/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.P.(Gen)Doc.1.Q.6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article 6</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1946-10-15T23:59:59+01:00" notBefore="1946-07-29T00:00:00+01:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Czechoslovakia proposes that a new article be inserted after Article 6, to run as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Wherever the date April 10th, 1941, figures in the present treaty, or
                            where it is a question of the commencement of the state of war, the date
                            November 2nd, 1938, is to apply in relations with Czechoslovakia.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Argument</hi>.</p>
                <p>As a result of the Vienna Award of November 2nd, 1938, part of Czechoslovakia was
                    occupied by Hungary. From the date onwards she considers that a state of war
                    existed between herself and Hungary, and is necessary that this fact should
                    receive political expression in the peace treaty.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
